    "question": "A manufacturing company runs 200 on-premises servers that upload telemetry to Amazon Kinesis Data Streams and Amazon S3. Each server currently holds long-term IAM access keys in a configuration file, and rotation is a manual quarterly task that has been missed twice. The company already operates a private certificate authority that issues X.509 certificates to every server, and the security team mandates that AWS authentication reuse those existing certificates and that all AWS credentials be temporary. Which solution meets these requirements?",
