    "question": "A financial services firm operates 60 accounts in AWS Organizations. Corporate policy states that the management account must host no workloads and that day-to-day sign-ins to it must be limited to a handful of billing and organization administrators. The security operations team needs organization-wide Amazon GuardDuty and AWS Security Hub coverage, with findings centralized in a dedicated security tooling account and every newly created account enrolled without manual steps. Which approach meets these requirements?",
