    "difficulty": "Hard",
    "type": "multiple",
    "question": "A logistics company allocates cloud spend to business units using a cost-center tag. Finance reports that roughly 30% of new EC2 instances and EBS volumes across the organization's 50 accounts are created without the tag or with misspelled variants such as CostCentre, making monthly chargeback unreliable. The governance team wants the tag key and its allowed values standardized across the organization and wants resource creation to fail outright when the tag is missing. Which combination of steps should a solutions architect take to meet these requirements? (Choose two.)",
    "options": [
      {
        "id": "a",
        "text": "Deploy the required-tags AWS Config managed rule to every member account with an automatic remediation action that stops noncompliant EC2 instances after they are detected.",
        "correct": false,
        "explanation": "Config rules are detective and act only after the resource exists, so untagged instances are still created and may run and accrue cost before remediation, which fails the requirement to block creation."
      },
      {
        "id": "b",
        "text": "Attach a tag policy to the organization root that defines the cost-center tag key with its case treatment and the list of allowed values for EC2 and EBS resource types.",
        "correct": true,
        "explanation": "Tag policies standardize the key spelling and permitted values organization-wide and surface noncompliant tags in compliance reporting, eliminating variants such as CostCentre."
      },
      {
        "id": "c",
        "text": "Use CloudFormation StackSets to apply IAM permissions boundaries in every account that require the cost-center tag key on all resource creation requests.",
        "correct": false,
        "explanation": "Permissions boundaries only affect principals they are attached to and must be maintained on every role in 50 accounts, leaving unbounded principals and new roles free to create untagged resources."
      },
      {
        "id": "d",
        "text": "Activate the cost-center key as a cost allocation tag from the billing console of each member account so it appears in the organization's chargeback reports.",
        "correct": false,
        "explanation": "Cost allocation tags are activated once from the management account payer, and activation only exposes the tag in billing data; it neither standardizes values nor blocks untagged creation."
      },
      {
        "id": "e",
        "text": "Attach an SCP to the workload OUs that denies ec2:RunInstances and ec2:CreateVolume when the aws:RequestTag/cost-center key is not present in the request.",
        "correct": true,
        "explanation": "Only an SCP provides the preventive control: the condition on aws:RequestTag rejects the API call itself whenever the cost-center tag is absent, so untagged resources can never be created."
      }
    ],
