    "difficulty": "Hard",
    "type": "single",
    "question": "An audit at a biotech company found that several of its 35 member accounts had no backups for DynamoDB tables and EBS volumes because account administrators had deleted or edited the AWS Backup plans that the platform team had deployed. A new mandate requires daily backups with 35-day retention for tagged resources in every account, requires that account administrators be unable to weaken the configuration, and must apply to accounts created in the future. Which solution meets these requirements?",
