    "service": "Amazon EBS",
    "difficulty": "Medium",
    "type": "single",
    "question": "The security team of an insurance company enabled EBS encryption by default with a customer managed KMS key in every account and Region of its organization. Three months later, an audit discovers 60 EBS volumes attached to long-running EC2 instances that are still unencrypted because they were created before the setting was enabled. The volumes host active application data and must be encrypted under the customer managed key with minimal disruption. What should the solutions architect do to bring these volumes into compliance?",
