    "question": "A publisher serves a static website from an S3 bucket through an Amazon CloudFront distribution. A penetration test produced two findings: requests sent to the CloudFront distribution over plain HTTP are served successfully without redirection, and an internal reporting tool retrieves objects directly from the bucket's S3 REST endpoint over HTTP. The compliance team requires that every access path to the content use TLS, while browsers that request the site over HTTP should still reach it rather than receive an error. Which combination of actions should the solutions architect take? (Choose two.)",
