    "type": "single",
    "question": "To satisfy a regulator's demand that all cryptographic key material be generated in the bank's own hardware security modules, a European bank imported external key material into a customer managed KMS key and set the material to expire in 12 months. The key currently protects three years of archived ciphertext that must remain decryptable for a further seven years. A newly hired solutions architect is documenting the key-management runbook. What should the architect include to ensure the archived data remains decryptable after the expiration date?",
