    "question": "An ad-tech platform writes roughly 500 million small objects per day to a single S3 bucket that uses SSE-KMS with a customer managed key, and analytics clusters read the objects back within hours. A cost review shows that AWS KMS request charges from these S3 operations have become one of the platform's largest line items. The security team insists that all objects continue to be encrypted with SSE-KMS under the existing customer managed key and that no application code changes be made. How can the solutions architect reduce the cost MOST effectively?",
