    "service": "Amazon S3",
    "difficulty": "Hard",
    "type": "single",
    "question": "A media company runs a licensing portal on Amazon ECS. A task role signs presigned GET URLs with a 12-hour expiration so studios can download master video files from a private S3 bucket. A studio reports that one of its download URLs was pasted into a public support forum 2 hours ago, and the security team has confirmed that the URL is still being used by unknown parties. The company must stop all further downloads through every outstanding presigned URL immediately, while keeping the portal able to issue new URLs after the incident is contained. What should a solutions architect do to meet these requirements?",
    "options": [
      {
        "id": "a",
        "text": "Enable all four S3 Block Public Access settings on the bucket so that every request made with the leaked presigned URL is rejected until its 12-hour expiration passes.",
        "correct": false,
        "explanation": "Block Public Access blocks anonymous and public grants, but a presigned URL is an authenticated request signed by the task role, so BPA does not stop it."
      },
      {
        "id": "b",
        "text": "Rotate the KMS key that encrypts the bucket so that requests made with the leaked URL can no longer decrypt the objects.",
        "correct": false,
        "explanation": "KMS key rotation keeps all prior key material usable for decryption, and the presigned request still decrypts through the signing role's permissions, so downloads continue."
      },
      {
        "id": "c",
        "text": "Attach an inline policy to the ECS task role that explicitly denies s3:GetObject on the bucket, then remove the deny after the incident is contained.",
        "correct": true,
        "explanation": "A presigned URL is re-evaluated against the signer's permissions at the time of each use, so an explicit deny on the signing role invalidates every outstanding URL at once and can be lifted later."
      },
      {
        "id": "d",
        "text": "Update the portal to sign all new presigned URLs with a 15-minute expiration so that the leaked URL ages out more quickly.",
        "correct": false,
        "explanation": "The expiration is fixed at signing time, so shortening it only affects URLs issued in the future and leaves the already-leaked 12-hour URL usable."
      }
    ],
