    "question": "A real-estate marketplace lets agents upload listing photos from a browser app. Uploads currently pass through an Auto Scaling group of EC2 proxy instances that validate files and forward them to S3, and the fleet's cost has tripled during a seasonal surge. The company wants browsers to upload directly to the bucket while still guaranteeing, before any object is stored, that each upload is no larger than 10 MB and has a Content-Type of image/jpeg. Which solution meets these requirements?",
