    "service": "AWS Shield Advanced",
    "difficulty": "Hard",
    "type": "multiple",
    "question": "A gaming company operates a session service that players reach over a custom TCP protocol through an internet-facing Network Load Balancer with Elastic IP addresses in three Availability Zones. Last quarter, a volumetric DDoS attack degraded gameplay for 40 minutes before the on-call engineer noticed, and the resulting Auto Scaling surge added several thousand dollars to the monthly bill. The company wants attack detection tuned to the application's actual health, direct access to AWS DDoS experts during attacks, and reimbursement for attack-driven scaling charges. Which combination of steps should a solutions architect take? (Choose two.)",
