    "explanation": "Each attack layer needs its own control: CloudFront moves the absorption point to the global edge and shields the origin, Shield Advanced supplies enhanced layer 3/4 mitigation plus DDoS cost protection, and WAF rate-based rules address the layer 7 request flood that network defenses cannot distinguish from legitimate traffic. Reactive NACL lists, in-VPC IPS appliances, and DNS Firewall all operate in the wrong place or at the wrong layer for internet-facing DDoS.",
