    "service": "Amazon Macie",
    "difficulty": "Hard",
    "type": "single",
    "question": "A media analytics company stores about 2 PB of data in an S3 data lake spread across 300 buckets. Roughly 40 buckets under a curated/ prefix hold customer records in CSV and JSON formats; the remaining buckets contain rendered video assets and application logs. Compliance must produce evidence within 30 days that the curated customer data contains no unmasked payment card numbers, and the CFO has already rejected a Macie estimate that priced a full-depth scan of the entire lake at several hundred thousand dollars. Which approach satisfies the compliance requirement MOST cost-effectively?",
    "options": [
      {
        "id": "a",
        "text": "Run a one-time Macie classification job across all 300 buckets with full-depth inspection so that no sensitive object anywhere in the lake is missed.",
        "correct": false,
        "explanation": "Scanning all 2 PB, including video assets and logs that cannot hold card numbers in scope, is exactly the full-lake estimate the CFO rejected and far exceeds what the audit asks for."
      },
      {
        "id": "b",
        "text": "Create a Macie classification job scoped to the 40 curated buckets, with object criteria for the curated/ prefix and CSV and JSON files and a sampling depth below 100 percent.",
        "correct": true,
        "explanation": "Bucket selection, object criteria, and sampling depth are Macie's cost levers; restricting the job to the buckets, prefix, and file types that can actually contain card data cuts inspected bytes by orders of magnitude while still producing audit evidence."
      },
      {
        "id": "c",
        "text": "Enable Macie automated sensitive data discovery for the account and rely on its ongoing sampling to eventually evaluate the objects across the data lake.",
        "correct": false,
        "explanation": "Automated discovery samples broadly and gradually to build a sensitivity map of all buckets; it does not target the curated data or guarantee coverage within the 30-day audit window."
      },
      {
        "id": "d",
        "text": "Generate S3 Inventory reports for the 40 curated buckets and run Athena queries with card-number regular expressions against the exported inventory data to produce the audit evidence.",
        "correct": false,
        "explanation": "S3 Inventory lists object metadata such as keys, sizes, and encryption status; it never contains object contents, so no regex against it can find payment card numbers."
      }
    ],
    "answers": [
      "b"
    ],
    "correctOptionIds": [
      "b"
    ],
    "sourceCorrectOptionIds": [
      "b"
    ],
    "answerSummary": "Scope a Macie classification job to the 40 curated buckets with prefix and file-type object criteria and a reduced sampling depth.",
