    "type": "single",
    "question": "An engineering team at a utilities company already streams its organization trail's management events to a CloudWatch Logs log group in the security account. After a phishing attempt against an executive, the CISO mandates notification within about a minute whenever the root user signs in to the console or any principal fails console authentication more than 5 times in 5 minutes. The team is directed to build on the existing log pipeline rather than adopt an additional security service. Which solution meets these requirements?",
    "options": [
      {
        "id": "a",
        "text": "Create an EventBridge scheduled rule that runs an Athena query against the trail's S3 logs every 15 minutes and publishes any matches to an SNS topic.",
        "correct": false,
        "explanation": "A 15-minute polling cycle plus S3 delivery lag cannot satisfy a one-minute notification target, and it bypasses the CloudWatch Logs stream the team already operates."
      },
      {
        "id": "b",
        "text": "Create CloudWatch Logs metric filters for root sign-ins and failed ConsoleLogin events, and configure alarms with a 5-failure threshold that notify an SNS topic.",
        "correct": true,
        "explanation": "Metric filters evaluate the streamed trail events as they arrive, and alarms with a threshold of 5 failures in 5 minutes plus a root sign-in alarm deliver near-real-time paging using only the pipeline that already exists."
      },
      {
        "id": "c",
        "text": "Enable AWS Config managed rules that evaluate root credential usage and console sign-in failures, and configure the rules to publish compliance changes to an SNS topic.",
        "correct": false,
        "explanation": "Config evaluates the configuration state of resources; sign-in events are activity, not configuration, so no Config rule can count console authentication failures."
      },
      {
        "id": "d",
        "text": "Enable GuardDuty in the security account so its root credential usage finding and brute-force detections flow through EventBridge to an SNS topic that pages the team.",
        "correct": false,
        "explanation": "GuardDuty is an additional security service, which the direction explicitly excludes, and its detections do not expose a configurable 5-failures-in-5-minutes threshold."
      }
    ],
    "answers": [
      "b"
    ],
    "correctOptionIds": [
      "b"
    ],
    "sourceCorrectOptionIds": [
      "b"
    ],
    "answerSummary": "Add CloudWatch Logs metric filters for root sign-ins and failed console logins with alarms to SNS on the existing log group.",
