    "question": "A healthcare company must migrate a 4 TB on-premises Oracle database to Amazon RDS for PostgreSQL using AWS DMS across an existing AWS Direct Connect link. Regulations require that replicated patient data be encrypted in transit between the database endpoints and the replication instance, and that any data staged on the replication instance be encrypted at rest with a KMS key the company created and controls. Which combination of steps meets these requirements? (Choose two.)",
