    "type": "single",
    "question": "A company centralizes backups with AWS Backup in a dedicated account. A backup operations team must be able to create backup plans, assign resources, and monitor job status, but compliance rules state that this team must never be able to restore recovery points or read the data it protects. A separate restore team performs all recoveries. Which solution enforces this separation of duties?",
