    "question": "A media company runs a video transcoding fleet in an Auto Scaling group across three Availability Zones. Worker instances pull jobs from an Amazon SQS queue, and a single transcode can take up to 20 minutes to complete. The group scales in aggressively during off-peak hours, and engineers have found that scale-in events terminate instances mid-transcode, forcing jobs to restart and delaying customer deliveries. The company wants terminating instances to finish their current job before shutting down while still allowing the fleet to scale in automatically. Which solution meets these requirements?",
