    "question": "An e-commerce company runs an Aurora MySQL cluster with one writer and two Aurora Replicas spread across three Availability Zones. The application's write path connects to the writer's instance endpoint, which an engineer copied from the console during initial setup. During a recent failover, one of the replicas was promoted to writer, and the application's writes failed with read-only errors until an engineer updated the configuration by hand. The company wants writes to keep working through future failovers without any configuration changes. Which change should a solutions architect recommend?",
