    "question": "A payments company protects its EC2-based transaction platform with AWS Elastic Disaster Recovery replicating into a recovery Region. A new compliance mandate requires quarterly disaster recovery game days that prove the platform can actually be recovered. The operations lead insists the tests must not affect production traffic and must not interrupt ongoing replication, because the replication lag alarm pages the on-call engineer. How should the solutions architect run the game days?",
