    "question": "A healthcare SaaS provider centralizes EBS, RDS, and DynamoDB backups with AWS Backup in its production account in eu-west-1. A security review concluded that an attacker with administrator access to the production account could delete both the live data and every recovery point, and that a Regional outage would leave no usable copies. The company must keep recoverable backups outside both the production account and the primary Region. Which combination of steps meets these requirements? (Choose two.)",
