    "question": "An online ticketing company stores orders in an Amazon RDS for PostgreSQL database that is protected by an AWS Backup plan taking snapshots every 6 hours. Last month a faulty deployment corrupted thousands of rows, and restoring the most recent snapshot discarded almost 5 hours of orders. The business has now set a firm tolerance of no more than 15 minutes of data loss when recovering from data corruption. Which change to the backup strategy meets this requirement?",
