    "question": "A retailer used AWS Elastic Disaster Recovery to fail its order-processing platform over to us-west-2 after a prolonged service disruption in us-east-1. The platform has now run in us-west-2 for nine days and has accumulated significant new order data. The primary Region is healthy again, and the company wants to return operations to us-east-1 without losing the orders taken during the event, and then restore its original disaster recovery posture. Which approach meets these requirements?",
