    "sourceCorrectOptionIds": [
      "c"
    ],
    "answerSummary": "Enable high-throughput FIFO and partition messages into groups by event ID.",
    "explanation": "FIFO throughput and ordering are both scoped to the message group, so a single group caps the queue at its per-group limit no matter how it is polled. Enabling high throughput mode and using the event ID as the message group ID distributes load across partitions while keeping strict order where it matters — within each event. Standard queues, queue sharding, and batching either sacrifice ordering guarantees or fall short of the target rate.",
