        "text": "Attach an Amazon SQS dead-letter queue to each HTTPS subscription so notifications that exhaust retries are captured and can be sent after the endpoint recovers.",
        "correct": true,
        "explanation": "A subscription-level DLQ durably stores any notification SNS could not deliver after all retries, so nothing is lost during outages longer than the retry window and the messages can be redriven afterward."
