    "service": "Amazon EventBridge",
    "difficulty": "Hard",
    "type": "multiple",
    "question": "A logistics company routes shipment events from a custom Amazon EventBridge bus to an AWS Step Functions state machine through a rule target. After an IAM policy change accidentally removed the rule's permission to start executions, EventBridge retried each event for up to 24 hours and then dropped it, and the loss went unnoticed for two days. The company requires that events are never lost when target invocation fails and that the operations team is notified of delivery failures within minutes. Which combination of steps should a solutions architect take? (Choose two.)",
