    "difficulty": "Medium",
    "type": "single",
    "question": "A fleet of containerized workers polls an Amazon SQS standard queue for pricing-update messages using the default ReceiveMessage settings. The team observes that many ReceiveMessage calls return no messages even when the queue is not empty, that some messages wait several seconds before any worker picks them up, and that the monthly bill shows millions of empty receive requests. The workers must pick up new messages with minimal delay while the request costs are reduced. What should a solutions architect recommend?",
