    "question": "A healthcare company recently enabled cross-Region replication on a bucket that has accumulated patient imaging files for ten years, replicating to a destination bucket in its disaster recovery Region. A DR readiness review finds two gaps: the millions of objects uploaded before the replication rule was created do not exist in the destination, and objects that a legacy ingestion service uploads with customer-provided encryption keys (SSE-C) are never replicated. Which combination of steps should a solutions architect take to close both gaps? (Choose two.)",
