    "question": "A logistics company runs an AWS Storage Gateway Volume Gateway in cached volumes mode on a VMware host in its distribution center, exposing three iSCSI volumes to local warehouse applications and taking scheduled snapshots of each volume every four hours. The VMware host suffers an unrecoverable hardware failure, destroying the gateway virtual machine along with its cache and upload buffer disks. The company must restore the applications' access to the volume data as quickly as possible. What should a solutions architect do?",
