    "question": "A payments company exposes a proprietary TCP API from Network Load Balancers in us-east-1 and eu-west-1. Its largest enterprise customers connect from corporate data centers whose DNS resolvers are known to cache records for hours regardless of the published 30-second TTL. During a recent regional incident, Route 53 failover updated DNS within a minute, but many customers continued sending traffic to the failed Region for most of the day. The company requires future regional failovers to take effect for all clients in under one minute. What should a solutions architect recommend?",
