    "question": "A gaming company stores player scores in a DynamoDB global table replicated across us-east-1, eu-west-1, and ap-northeast-1. Match servers in each Region execute UpdateItem calls with an ADD expression to increment a player's lifetime points on the same item. Players who compete in tournaments hosted in different Regions within the same minute report lifetime totals that are lower than the sum of their match awards, and the discrepancy grows during peak hours. All writes succeed without errors. What should a solutions architect do to ensure every increment is reflected in the total?",
