    "question": "A stock exchange operates matching engines in two Regions in an active-standby topology. After an automated DNS health check once shifted production to the standby Region during a harmless deployment, regulators now require that regional failover occur only through an explicit operator decision with an audit trail, and that it be technically impossible to turn off both Regions at once. The failover mechanism itself must remain usable even when the primary Region's control plane is impaired. Which solution meets these requirements?",
