    "service": "ACM",
    "difficulty": "Hard",
    "type": "multiple",
    "question": "A travel company is deploying its booking site at www.example.com behind a single Amazon CloudFront distribution. The distribution's origins are Application Load Balancers in us-west-2 and ap-southeast-2, selected through an origin group for failover. Security policy requires HTTPS on every hop: from viewers to CloudFront using the custom domain, and from CloudFront to each regional origin. The team uses AWS Certificate Manager for all certificates. Which combination of steps should a solutions architect take to satisfy the TLS requirements? (Choose two.)",
    "options": [
      {
        "id": "a",
        "text": "Request an ACM certificate for www.example.com in us-east-1 and associate that certificate with the CloudFront distribution's custom domain configuration.",
        "correct": true,
        "explanation": "CloudFront is a global service that only accepts ACM certificates issued in us-east-1, so the viewer-facing certificate for the custom domain must live in that Region."
      },
      {
        "id": "b",
        "text": "Request an ACM certificate for www.example.com in us-west-2 and associate that certificate with the CloudFront distribution's custom domain configuration.",
        "correct": false,
        "explanation": "A certificate issued in us-west-2 cannot be attached to a CloudFront distribution; the console and API only list certificates from us-east-1 for CloudFront use."
      },
      {
        "id": "c",
        "text": "Request a single ACM certificate in us-east-1 and export its private key for installation on the load balancers in us-west-2 and ap-southeast-2 to cover the origin connections.",
        "correct": false,
        "explanation": "Public ACM certificates cannot be exported because ACM never releases their private keys, so one certificate cannot be manually installed onto load balancers in other Regions."
      },
      {
        "id": "d",
        "text": "Request separate ACM certificates for the origin domain names in us-west-2 and ap-southeast-2 and attach each one to the HTTPS listener of the load balancer in its Region.",
        "correct": true,
        "explanation": "ACM certificates for load balancers are Regional resources, so each ALB needs a certificate issued in its own Region covering the origin hostname CloudFront connects to."
      },
      {
        "id": "e",
        "text": "Request an ACM certificate in ap-southeast-2 and attach that single certificate to the HTTPS listeners of the load balancers in both us-west-2 and ap-southeast-2.",
        "correct": false,
        "explanation": "An ACM certificate can only be associated with resources in the Region where it was issued, so a certificate from ap-southeast-2 cannot serve a load balancer in us-west-2."
      }
    ],
