    "question": "A media company is migrating a content-distribution node from an aging instance type to new hardware. The node must sustain more than 12 Gbps of traffic to downstream instances in the same VPC. The instance still boots from an AMI originally imported from the company's data center in 2015, and initial tests on the new instance type show network throughput far below expectations. What should a solutions architect do to ensure the node can reach the required network performance?",
