    "question": "An analytics team runs a pool of r6i.2xlarge development instances that each load a 55 GiB reference dataset into an in-memory lookup cache. Building the cache takes about 40 minutes after every boot. The instances are needed only between 8 AM and 6 PM on weekdays, and finance wants them off overnight to cut costs, but the team refuses any solution that makes the cache rebuild delay the start of the workday. Which approach satisfies both requirements MOST cost-effectively?",
