    "question": "An ad-tech company runs a stateless bidding fleet in an Auto Scaling group whose launch template overrides list exactly three instance types: c5.2xlarge, c5a.2xlarge, and c6i.2xlarge. During regional demand surges the group repeatedly fails to scale out because all three types return InsufficientInstanceCapacity errors in one Availability Zone, and on-call engineers respond by manually appending newer compatible types to the list. The workload runs correctly on any current x86 instance with at least 8 vCPUs and 16 GiB of memory. How can the company keep capacity available during shortages with the LEAST operational overhead?",
