    "difficulty": "Hard",
    "type": "single",
    "question": "A streaming platform operates a self-managed Apache Kafka cluster of nine broker instances with a replication factor of three. Inter-broker replication latency requirements keep all brokers in a single Availability Zone. Last month a rack-level hardware failure took down three brokers that happened to share underlying infrastructure, simultaneously destroying two of the three replicas for several topic partitions. The team wants EC2 placement that isolates groups of brokers on distinct hardware and exposes the topology so replicas can be assigned to different failure domains. Which placement approach meets these requirements?",
