    "question": "A payments company stores account balances in an Amazon DynamoDB table. The workload is about 70% writes, and a compliance mandate requires every balance read to use strongly consistent reads. The table is experiencing throttling during end-of-day settlement, and a developer proposes adding a DynamoDB Accelerator (DAX) cluster to improve performance. How should a solutions architect respond?",
