    "question": "A gaming company runs player session state on an Amazon ElastiCache for Redis replication group with cluster mode disabled: one cache.r6g.2xlarge primary and two read replicas. The primary's EngineCPUUtilization holds at 95% during evening play, driven almost entirely by write commands, and write latency is climbing. Traffic is forecast to triple next quarter. Which combination of steps should a solutions architect take to scale write throughput? (Choose three.)",
