    "question": "A news application serves images and article content through a CloudFront distribution configured for HTTP/2. Analytics show that commuting readers on cellular networks frequently switch between Wi-Fi and mobile data, and each switch drops the TCP connection, forcing a new TLS handshake and stalling in-progress downloads. The team wants to reduce these stalls for supported clients without changing the application or the origin. Which change will BEST reduce the interruptions?",
