    "question": "An ad-tech company ingests bid events into a provisioned Amazon Kinesis Data Streams stream with 10 shards. Baseline traffic is 4 MB/s and about 3,000 records per second, but when advertisers launch campaigns, traffic spikes to 35 MB/s within minutes and producers begin receiving ProvisionedThroughputExceededException errors. Campaign launch times are decided by customers and cannot be predicted, and the data platform team does not want to maintain capacity forecasts or scaling scripts for the stream. What should a solutions architect recommend to handle the spikes with the LEAST operational overhead?",
