    "question": "An industrial IoT platform sends 60,000 sensor readings per second, each about 150 bytes, into a provisioned Amazon Kinesis Data Streams stream. Total data volume is only about 9 MB/s, but producers are throttled because the stream's 12 shards allow a combined 12,000 records per second. The platform team wants to stop the throttling without expanding the stream to the roughly 60 shards that the record rate alone would require. What should a solutions architect recommend?",
