    "question": "A payments company runs a transactional database on an EC2 instance backed by a 2 TB io1 volume provisioned with 20,000 IOPS. Three months of CloudWatch metrics show the volume peaking at roughly 3,000 IOPS and 250 MB/s of throughput, about 15% of what is provisioned, with no upward trend. The database must remain online during any storage change. Which action reduces the volume cost the MOST while still meeting the measured performance?",
