        "id": "b",
        "text": "Migrate the volume to io2 at the same 20,000 provisioned IOPS to benefit from the newer generation's pricing and higher durability.",
        "correct": false,
        "explanation": "Staying at 20,000 IOPS preserves the core waste of paying for nearly seven times the observed peak, and the added durability was never a stated requirement of the workload."
