    "question": "An insurance company's payer account shows that 30% of monthly spend cannot be attributed to any cost center. Investigation found two causes: several teams applied a CostCenter tag that never appears in billing data, and many other resources were never tagged at all. Leadership wants a monthly report in which every dollar is either mapped to a business unit or explicitly called out as unattributed, together with a repeatable process that drives the unattributed share toward zero over the next several quarters. Which combination of steps should a solutions architect take to meet these requirements? (Choose three.)",
